  "tldr": "Testing whether a conditional average treatment effect is constant is an omnibus signal-detection problem whose difficulty may change when propensity and baseline functions are rough. The project first identifies CATE variance with a profiled inverse-free conditional score, proves the supplied-propensity benchmark, and develops a total higher-order projection test with a uniform achievability envelope. Its central open result is the same-class minimax converse under exactly uniform covariates and an unknown constant-effect composite null. Closing that converse, or using its obstruction to improve the test, yields the first explicit phase diagram showing exactly when learning observational confounding changes the smooth CATE detection boundary.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Existing constant-CATE procedures establish asymptotic validity, fixed-alternative consistency, or power conditional on a learned direction and nuisance-rate assumptions. The closest H\u00f6lder minimax causal result concerns pointwise CATE estimation, and its lower-bound construction removes covariate mass from transition regions, which is illegal under the present exactly uniform design.",
    "niche": "The unresolved object is a full-class minimax separation radius that simultaneously accounts for CATE approximation bias, propensity-baseline interaction bias, quadratic-energy variance, correction variance, unknown constant profiling, and legal observed-data indistinguishability when first-order product rates fail.",
    "fill": "An inverse-free score reduction and finite local-polynomial higher-order U-statistic give a computable upper envelope. A full-support, null-preserving mixture program either matches every envelope branch or exposes an observable discrepancy that can be used to sharpen the upper construction, producing the exact nuisance-penalty phase diagram without assuming its exponent."
  },
  "related_work": "Dhawan, Guo, and Shah motivate effect-modifier testing and prove direction-dependent local power for a debiased hunt-and-test statistic; their Theorem 1 and Corollary 2 inform the scientific entry point but do not provide an omnibus H\u00f6lder radius. Yu targets CATE variance directly and proves Gaussian validity and fixed-alternative consistency under learner conditions, leaving rough-regime local separation open. Kennedy, Balakrishnan, Robins, and Wasserman provide the closest asymmetric-smoothness machinery: their Theorems 1 and 2 combine localized fuzzy hypotheses with higher-order CATE estimation, and their discussion explicitly names minimax CATE testing as future work. Ingster and Sapatinas supply the random-uniform-design truncated quadratic detector and mixture benchmark recovered in the supplied-propensity experiment. Robins, Li, Tchetgen Tchetgen, and van der Vaart supply the higher-order projection calculus adapted to cancel successive causal nuisance products. Lundborg, Kim, Shah, and Samworth prove a matched conditional-mean significance rate in a noncausal common-smoothness model; the first changed step here is joint control of the profiled causal score and the propensity-baseline correction. Hines, Diaz-Ordaz, and Vansteelandt identify treatment-effect variable-importance energies and regular inference away from degeneracy, while S\u00e1nchez-Becerra treats boundary-sensitive VCATE inference in experiments. Crump, Hotz, Imbens, and Mitnik provide the foundational sieve test of constant CATE but not a sharp rough-confounding separation frontier.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "The candidate achievability exponent in Theorem 5 depends on \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\) only through \\(s_0=\\alpha+\\beta\\); this is not asserted to be the sharp minimax dependence. The first destructive check is \\(d=1\\), \\(\\alpha=1/64\\), \\(\\beta=9/64\\), and \\(\\gamma=1/8\\), where the optimized ranks exceed \\(n\\), the nuisance rank is below the signal rank, and the baseline is smoother than the CATE. Transition-region mass, baseline smoothness, or joint coefficient covariance may invalidate a matching converse at the achievability scale. A failed prior construction is not evidence of a nuisance penalty.",
  "honest_scope": "The score identity, profiled-energy equivalence, legal witness, supplied-propensity benchmark, and projection-correction upper envelope are precise claims to prove. The exact observational exponent, its individual dependence on \\(\\alpha\\) and \\(\\beta\\), every equality-case logarithm, and the legal full-support converse remain open. Under the special case \\(e_P\\equiv1/2\\) and \\(\\mu_{P,0}\\equiv1/2\\), the problem reduces to the known random-design quadratic-detection benchmark. No claim is made for unknown covariate density, vanishing overlap, adaptive smoothness, continuous ACTG175 outcomes, or retrospective changes to published empirical \\(p\\)-values."
